{
  "name": "Register",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "register_id": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "name": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "location": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "status": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "online",
        "offline",
        "maintenance"
      ],
      "default": "offline"
    },
    "ip_address": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "subnet_mask": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "gateway": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "assigned_operator": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "feature_returns": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false,
      "description": "Enable Returns / Refunds on this register"
    },
    "feature_customer_service": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false,
      "description": "Enable Customer Service Mode on this register"
    },
    "feature_exchange": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false,
      "description": "Enable Item Exchange on this register"
    },
    "paused": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false,
      "description": "Whether this register is paused (locked from use)"
    },
    "remote_logout_requested": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false,
      "description": "Flag indicating a remote logout has been requested by admin"
    },
    "remote_logout_reason": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Reason for remote logout to display on POS"
    },
    "remote_logout_requested_at": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "When the remote logout was requested (used for 10-minute auto-logout)"
    },
    "cash_limit": {
      "type": "number",
      "default": 5000,
      "description": "Maximum cash allowed in register drawer before audit required"
    },
    "printer_status": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "connected",
        "disconnected",
        "unknown"
      ],
      "default": "unknown",
      "description": "Receipt printer connectivity status"
    },
    "scanner_status": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "connected",
        "disconnected",
        "unknown"
      ],
      "default": "unknown",
      "description": "Barcode scanner connectivity status"
    },
    "cash_drawer_status": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "connected",
        "disconnected",
        "unknown"
      ],
      "default": "unknown",
      "description": "Cash drawer connectivity status"
    },
    "printer_model": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Receipt printer make/model connected to this register"
    },
    "printer_ip": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Address the relay sends this lane's receipts and cash-drawer kick to on port 9100. Ethernet transport = the printer's own LAN IP (e.g. 192.168.1.60). USB transport = the LANE's own LAN IP, because the lane's socat bridge publishes the USB printer on port 9100. Blank = the relay uses the first printer in its PRINTER_IPS list."
    },
    "printer_transport": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "ethernet",
        "usb_bridge"
      ],
      "default": "ethernet",
      "description": "How the relay reaches this lane's receipt printer. ethernet = the printer's own embedded network interface; usb_bridge = the printer is USB-attached to the lane (Epson UB-U06) and published on the lane's IP by the socat printer bridge, giving a single uplink cable per lane. The relay code is identical either way \u2014 only printer_ip changes."
    },
    "printer_fallback_ip": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The printer's embedded Ethernet IP, kept cabled and live at the same time as USB (the TM-H6000IV serves both interfaces concurrently). If the lane's USB bridge or the lane itself fails, an admin pastes this into printer_ip to recover instantly with no hardware swap or site visit."
    },
    "scanner_model": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Barcode scanner make/model connected to this register (e.g. Zebra DS4308)"
    },
    "cash_drawer_model": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Cash drawer make/model connected to this register"
    },
    "printer_serial": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Receipt printer serial number"
    },
    "scanner_serial": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Barcode scanner serial number"
    },
    "cash_drawer_serial": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Cash drawer serial number"
    },
    "drawer_transport": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "printer_dk",
        "usb_direct"
      ],
      "default": "printer_dk",
      "description": "How this lane's cash drawer is fired. printer_dk = the fleet standard: the drawer hangs off the receipt printer's DK (RJ11/SDL) port and the printer's controller fires the 24V pulse when the POS sends ESC p to printer_ip \u2014 transport-agnostic, so it works with an Ethernet printer or a USB-bridged one. usb_direct = RESERVED: a native USB drawer plugged into the lane, published on the lane's drawer bridge port, driven by the drawer model's own open command. usb_direct exists so a discontinued SDL drawer can be replaced with its USB sibling without moving the whole fleet to off-brand RJ11 drawers; it requires the lane's drawer bridge in the image."
    },
    "drawer_bridge_ip": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Address the relay sends a USB drawer's open command to. Blank = the lane's own ip_address, matching how the USB printer, pole and pinpad bridges work. Only used when drawer_transport is usb_direct."
    },
    "drawer_bridge_port": {
      "type": "number",
      "default": 9102,
      "description": "TCP port the lane's USB drawer bridge listens on. Sits alongside the other lane bridges (9100 printer, 9101 pole, 12000 pinpad). Only used when drawer_transport is usb_direct."
    },
    "drawer_model": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Native USB drawer model, matched against a HardwareLibrary cash_drawer profile to get its open command. Blank = the standard ESC p pulse. Only used when drawer_transport is usb_direct."
    },
    "terminal_model": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "POS terminal / computer make and model (e.g. IBM SurePOS 700, Elo EPS00E2)"
    },
    "terminal_serial": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "POS terminal / computer serial number"
    },
    "mac_address": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Primary NIC MAC address of the terminal. Used as the hardware identity for PXE/diskless boot instead of a static IP."
    },
    "boot_profile": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "pxe_debian_legacy",
        "pxe_debian_modern",
        "local_disk"
      ],
      "default": "local_disk",
      "description": "Which boot image the store's PXE controller serves this terminal. pxe_debian_legacy = IBM SurePOS 700 class hardware; pxe_debian_modern = Elo EPS00E2 class hardware; local_disk = terminal boots from its own disk."
    },
    "keyboard_model": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "POS keyboard make/model (e.g. IBM 3AA01194300). Determines the udev/hwdb scancode mapping applied at boot."
    },
    "scanner_interface": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "usb_hid",
        "rs232_serial",
        "usb_ocia",
        "unknown"
      ],
      "default": "usb_hid",
      "description": "How the barcode scanner attaches to the terminal. usb_hid = keyboard-wedge (Zebra DS4308 default); rs232_serial / usb_ocia = legacy IBM interfaces requiring extra driver setup."
    },
    "pinpad_model": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "",
        "isc250",
        "lane_7000"
      ],
      "default": "",
      "description": "Customer-facing Ingenico pinpad attached to this lane. Selects the command profile the relay uses to drive it: isc250 = Ingenico iSC Touch 250 (supported today, over Ethernet or USB \u2014 a USB pad is reached through the lane's serial bridge on port 12000), lane_7000 = Ingenico Lane/7000 (profile reserved for a future rollout). Blank = no pinpad on this lane, and every pinpad prompt is skipped silently."
    },
    "pinpad_ip": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "LAN IP the relay drives this lane's pinpad on. Ethernet pad = the pad's own IP (e.g. 192.168.1.70). USB pad = the LANE's own LAN IP, because the lane's ser2net serial bridge publishes the pad on port 12000. Drives signature capture, customer prompts, gift-card entry, the cart mirror and the rating screen."
    },
    "pinpad_serial": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Pinpad serial number, for the hardware audit."
    },
    "pole_display_model": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "",
        "epson_dmd110",
        "ibm_4610_2x20",
        "toshiba_4820_2x20",
        "toshiba_usb_2x20",
        "logic_ld9900"
      ],
      "default": "",
      "description": "Customer-facing pole display (line display) on this lane. Selects the command profile and transport the relay uses. SUPPORTED TODAY: epson_dmd110 = Epson DM-D110 driven pass-through via the lane's receipt printer. RESERVED (not yet supported \u2014 a lane assigned one behaves as if no pole is fitted): ibm_4610_2x20 / toshiba_4820_2x20 = IBM and Toshiba 2x20 poles on the 4610/4820 RS-485 device chain, awaiting frame capture from a live unit with the pole capture helper; toshiba_usb_2x20 = Toshiba TCx 2x20 USB pole (0f66:4524), reserved pending USB protocol capture \u2014 the Toshiba VSP driver was proven on a live lane NOT to translate its HID framing (vsd only symlinks the raw hidraw device), so no transport currently reaches it; logic_ld9900 = Logic Controls LD9900 over a serial-device server. Blank or a reserved profile = every display update is skipped silently."
    },
    "pole_display_ip": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "LAN IP the relay writes pole display frames to. Leave blank for the DM-D110 and the IBM / Toshiba RS-485 chain poles \u2014 they hang off the receipt printer and the relay routes through printer_ip. Set it to the LANE's own LAN IP for a USB pole (the lane's serial bridge publishes it on port 9101), or to the device's own address for a pole on a serial-device server."
    },
    "pole_display_serial": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Pole display serial number, for the hardware audit."
    },
    "customer_monitor_enabled": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false,
      "description": "True when this lane has a second, customer-facing MONITOR fitted (not a pole). Deliberately separate from pole_display_model so a lane can run a pole, a monitor, or both \u2014 the pole profiles remain the reserve path while their serial/HID protocols are still being captured. When on, the lane's boot entry carries sureflow.customer_monitor=1 and the kiosk launcher opens a second fullscreen Chromium window on the second Xorg output at /customer-display?register_id=... The monitor is purely informational: payment, PIN and signature stay on the Ingenico pinpad."
    },
    "customer_monitor_resolution": {
      "type": "string",
      "default": "1920x1080",
      "description": "Native resolution of the customer panel (e.g. 1920x1080). Used to size the combined X screen's Virtual line \u2014 too small a Virtual is the classic dual-head failure, where X starts, the operator panel is perfect and the customer panel is black with nothing at all in the Xorg log."
    },
    "customer_monitor_orientation": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "landscape",
        "portrait"
      ],
      "default": "landscape",
      "description": "Physical mounting of the customer panel. portrait adds a Rotate option to its Xorg Monitor section and swaps the width/height used for the combined framebuffer."
    },
    "customer_monitor_serial": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Customer monitor serial number, for the hardware audit."
    },
    "store_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Store number this register belongs to. POS reads this to scope all data to the store."
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "register_id",
    "name"
  ],
  "rls": {
    "create": {
      "user_condition": {
        "role": "admin"
      }
    },
    "read": null,
    "update": {
      "$or": [
        {
          "created_by_id": "{{user.id}}"
        },
        {
          "user_condition": {
            "role": "admin"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "delete": {
      "user_condition": {
        "role": "admin"
      }
    }
  }
}